cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Joint content recommendation and edge caching with deep RL"
abstract: >-
  Deep reinforcement learning for joint content recommendation and edge
  caching. A Double DQN agent jointly recommends the next content item and decides
  whether to admit the just-watched item into a single edge cache, trained
  and evaluated in a MovieLens-derived simulator. Compares joint learning
  against recommendation-only RL with heuristic caching, and against non-RL
  baselines. Post-graduation re-implementation of the author's diploma thesis
  (Technical University of Crete, 2025) with a redesigned Q-network and a
  faster training pipeline.
authors:
  - family-names: Alogoskoufis
    given-names: Alexandros
keywords:
  - deep reinforcement learning
  - recommendation systems
  - edge caching
  - content delivery
  - DQN
  - double-dqn
